#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * AURA — message search and friend streaks
 *
 *   - Messages gets a search box: words in all your chats (or "Only in" the one that's open), with
 *     the chat, who said it and the date; click a result to jump to that message.
 *   - Friend streaks: 🔥 and the number of days in a row you and a friend have both messaged (a
 *     call counts too), from 3 days, in your chats, the chat header and your friends lists. ⌛ in
 *     the evening if neither of you has messaged yet today.
 *   Nothing new is stored. The privacy policy says how both work.
 *
 *   Also run  supabase/aura-messages-search.sql  in Supabase (SQL Editor), once.
 *
 * How to use:  node aura-messages-search-setup.cjs      (in your AURA project folder)
 * To undo:     node aura-messages-search-setup.cjs --undo
 */
